<title>USA: Glickman-no ag impact with Mexico, Colombia status.</title>
<headline>Glickman-no ag impact with Mexico, Colombia status.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman said Friday that there will not likely be any impact on agricultural trade if the executive branch decides to decertify Mexico and Colombia because of their drug policies.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think so,&quot; Glickman said in answer to a reporter's question if trade would be hurt if there was a change in the status of those two countries.</p>
<p>Mexico, a member of NAFTA, is a large buyer of U.S. agricultural commodities, including feedgrains and livestock products.</p>
</text>
